---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro'

const FORM_ID = 'xaqlggla'
const DOWNLOAD_URL = '/reports/demand-collapse-mode-2.pdf'
---
<Base
  title="Failure Mode #2: They Find You and Leave | EngageEngine™"
  description="492 businesses. $77.4M in leaked revenue. They found your site. Something didn't give them enough confidence to engage. Download The Demand Collapse Report: Mode 2."
>
  <Nav />
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="diag-hero">
      <div class="diag-wrap">
        <span class="diag-eyebrow">Failure Mode #2 of 4</span>
        <h1>
          <span class="hero-word">They</span>
          <span class="hero-word"> found</span>
          <span class="hero-word"> you.</span>
          <span class="hero-word"> Then</span>
          <span class="hero-word"> left.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="diag-lead hero-sub">
          They were looking. They found your site. They read enough to know you probably do what they need. But something in the experience didn't give them enough confidence to take the next step. So they left — quietly, without telling you why.
        </p>
        <p class="diag-mechanism hero-sub">
          This isn't a traffic problem. It's not an SEO problem. The buyers arrived. Your site didn't convert the interest into contact. That's Gate 2.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Math -->
    <section class="diag-section">
      <div class="diag-wrap">
        <span class="diag-label" data-animate>The Demand Collapse Report — Mode 2</span>
        <p class="diag-context" data-animate data-delay="0.1">We diagnosed 2,400 businesses. 492 had this exact failure mode. Here's what it cost them.</p>
        <div class="math-stats" data-animate data-delay="0.15">
          <div class="math-stat">
            <span class="math-num" data-count="492" data-duration="1.8">492</span>
            <span class="math-desc">of 2,400 businesses diagnosed with Mode 2 failure — 20% of all cases</span>
          </div>
          <div class="math-stat">
            <span class="math-num" data-count="157309" data-duration="2" data-prefix="$">$157,309</span>
            <span class="math-desc">average annual revenue leaked per business. Range: $55K–$340K.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="math-stat math-stat-accent">
            <span class="math-num" data-count="77.4" data-duration="2.2" data-prefix="$" data-suffix="M" data-decimals="1">$77.4M</span>
            <span class="math-desc">total profit leaks found across all Mode 2 businesses. The buyers were real. The interest was real. The conversion system wasn't.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Sound Familiar -->
    <section class="diag-section">
      <div class="diag-wrap">
        <span class="diag-label" data-animate>Sound Familiar?</span>
        <div class="familiar-grid" data-animate data-delay="0.05">
          <div class="familiar-card">
            <p class="familiar-quote">"We get traffic. We just don't get calls. I've redesigned the site three times and it still doesn't convert."</p>
          </div>
          <div class="familiar-card">
            <p class="familiar-quote">"People find us on Google. They look at the site. They don't call. Then we see them on a competitor's truck two weeks later."</p>
          </div>
          <div class="familiar-card">
            <p class="familiar-quote">"Our bounce rate is terrible. We know something's wrong. We just don't know what to fix."</p>
          </div>
          <div class="familiar-card">
            <p class="familiar-quote">"The leads we do get are lower quality than they used to be. The serious buyers seem to go somewhere else."</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="familiar-note" data-animate data-delay="0.25">None of these are design problems. None are copy problems. They're a trust architecture problem. Buyers research quietly and decide fast — and your site isn't built for that moment.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Lie / The Truth -->
    <section class="diag-section">
      <div class="diag-wrap">
        <span class="diag-label" data-animate>The Lie. The Truth.</span>
        <div class="lt-grid" data-animate data-delay="0.05">
          <div class="lt-row">
            <div class="lt-lie">
              <span class="lt-tag lt-tag-lie">The Lie</span>
              <p>"We need a better website design."</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lt-truth">
              <span class="lt-tag lt-tag-truth">The Truth</span>
              <p>Design influences trust, but a prettier site doesn't fix missing proof. Buyers don't bounce because your colors are wrong. They bounce because they can't answer "why should I trust these people?" in the first 30 seconds. That's a proof problem, not a design problem.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="lt-row">
            <div class="lt-lie">
              <span class="lt-tag lt-tag-lie">The Lie</span>
              <p>"We need more case studies."</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lt-truth">
              <span class="lt-tag lt-tag-truth">The Truth</span>
              <p>Case studies help later in the decision. They don't create initial confidence. Credibility signals need to be immediate and ambient — not buried in a resource library someone has to find. If they leave before they find your proof, more proof doesn't help.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="lt-row">
            <div class="lt-lie">
              <span class="lt-tag lt-tag-lie">The Lie</span>
              <p>"We need more reviews on Google."</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lt-truth">
              <span class="lt-tag lt-tag-truth">The Truth</span>
              <p>More reviews help if people are reading them. But the trust gap is being hit at first impression — not at validation. If visitors leave before reviews matter, more reviews change nothing. Fix the top of the experience first.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PDF Download Gate -->
    <section class="gate-section">
      <div class="gate-inner">
        <div class="gate-left" data-animate>
          <span class="diag-label">The Demand Collapse Report</span>
          <h2 class="gate-heading">Mode 2 Failure:<br/>Seen But Not Trusted.</h2>
          <p class="gate-body">5-page report. The Gate 2 trust architecture diagram, the math on what businesses with this failure mode lose annually, and the three wrong fixes most teams try first.</p>
          <ul class="gate-list">
            <li>The Gate 2 diagram — where trust breaks down in the buyer's journey</li>
            <li>The math — what Mode 2 businesses leak annually vs. what they could recover</li>
            <li>The three wrong fixes and why they don't address the real gap</li>
            <li>What Trust Architecture actually requires — and what to build first</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="gate-sub">No sequence. No sales call. Just the report.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gate-right" data-animate data-delay="0.1">
          <form id="gate-form" class="gate-form">
            <div class="form-row">
              <label class="form-label">Full Name</label>
              <input type="text" name="name" required  class="form-input" />
            </div>
            <div class="form-row">
              <label class="form-label">Email Address</label>
              <input type="email" name="email" required  class="form-input" />
            </div>
            <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="Mode 2 Report Download" />
            <input type="hidden" name="failure_mode" value="Mode 2 — Seen But Not Trusted" />
            <button type="submit" class="gate-btn">Download the Report →</button>
            <p id="gate-error" class="gate-error hidden">Something went wrong. Please try again.</p>
          </form>
          <div id="gate-success" class="gate-success hidden">
            <p class="success-heading">Your download is starting.</p>
            <p class="success-body">If it doesn't start automatically, <a href={DOWNLOAD_URL} class="success-link">click here</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Bottom CTA -->
    <section class="bottom-cta" data-animate>
      <div class="bottom-cta-inner">
        <p class="diag-label">Not sure this is your failure mode?</p>
        <h3 class="bottom-heading">12 questions finds it.</h3>
        <a href="/diagnostic/" class="btn btn-blue">Take the Free Diagnostic →</a>
        <p class="bottom-sub">12 questions. No sales call. Takes 4 minutes.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .diag-hero { background: var(--canvas); padding: 80px 22px 72px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .diag-wrap { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .diag-section { padding: 80px 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--white); }
  .diag-section:nth-child(odd) { background: var(--canvas); }

  .diag-eyebrow { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--blue); display: block; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .diag-hero h1 { font-family: var(--font-d); font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 68px); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -0.005em; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .hero-word { display: inline-block; }
  .diag-lead { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.6; letter-spacing: -0.022em; color: var(--mid-gray); max-width: 680px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .diag-mechanism { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--mid-gray); max-width: 520px; padding-left: 16px; border-left: 3px solid var(--blue); }

  .diag-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--blue); display: block; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .diag-context { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--mid-gray); margin-bottom: 40px; max-width: 560px; }

  .math-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--border); }
  .math-stat { background: var(--white); padding: 36px 28px; }
  .math-stat-accent { background: var(--canvas); }
  .math-num { font-family: var(--font-d); font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); font-weight: 700; color: var(--blue); display: block; margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .math-desc { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--mid-gray); }

  .familiar-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1px; background: var(--border); margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .familiar-card { background: var(--white); padding: 32px; }
  .familiar-quote { font-family: var(--font-d); font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; color: var(--graphite); line-height: 1.6; }
  .familiar-note { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--mid-gray); line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 16px; border-left: 3px solid rgba(0,113,227,0.3); max-width: 620px; }

  .lt-grid { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px; background: var(--border); }
  .lt-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr; gap: 1px; background: var(--border); }
  .lt-lie { background: var(--canvas); padding: 32px 28px; }
  .lt-truth { background: var(--white); padding: 32px 28px; }
  .lt-tag { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; display: block; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .lt-tag-lie { color: #c0392b; }
  .lt-tag-truth { color: var(--blue); }
  .lt-lie p { font-family: var(--font-d); font-size: 17px; font-style: italic; color: var(--mid-gray); line-height: 1.5; }
  .lt-truth p { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--mid-gray); }

  .gate-section { padding: 80px 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--canvas); }
  .gate-inner { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 64px; align-items: start; }
  .gate-heading { font-family: var(--font-d); font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px); font-weight: 600; color: var(--graphite); line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 16px; letter-spacing: -0.005em; }
  .gate-body { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--mid-gray); margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .gate-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .gate-list li { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--mid-gray); padding-left: 18px; position: relative; line-height: 1.6; }
  .gate-list li::before { content: '→'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--blue); font-size: 12px; }
  .gate-sub { font-size: 12px; color: var(--light-gray); letter-spacing: 0.04em; }

  .gate-form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }
  .form-row { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
  .form-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mid-gray); }
  .form-input { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--graphite); font-family: var(--font-t); font-size: 15px; padding: 12px 14px; outline: none; transition: border-color 0.2s; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .form-input::placeholder { color: var(--light-gray); }
  .form-input:focus { border-color: var(--blue); }
  .gate-btn { background: var(--blue); color: var(--white); font-family: var(--font-t); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; padding: 14px 24px; border: none; cursor: pointer; text-align: left; transition: background 0.2s; letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
  .gate-btn:hover { background: var(--blue-link); }
  .gate-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: not-allowed; }
  .gate-error { font-size: 13px; color: #c0392b; }
  .gate-success { padding: 24px 0 0; }
  .success-heading { font-family: var(--font-d); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .success-body { font-size: 14px; color: var(--mid-gray); }
  .success-link { color: var(--blue-link); text-decoration: none; }
  .success-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .hidden { display: none !important; }

  .bottom-cta { padding: 80px 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--white); text-align: center; }
  .bottom-cta-inner { max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .bottom-heading { font-family: var(--font-d); font-size: clamp(26px, 3vw, 36px); font-weight: 600; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 24px; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.005em; }
  .bottom-sub { font-size: 13px; color: var(--light-gray); margin-top: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.02em; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .math-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .familiar-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .lt-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .gate-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }
    .diag-hero { padding: 52px 16px 52px; }
  }
</style>

<script define:vars={{ FORM_ID, DOWNLOAD_URL }}>
  const form = document.getElementById('gate-form')
  const errorMsg = document.getElementById('gate-error')
  const successMsg = document.getElementById('gate-success')

  if (form) {
    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault()
      const btn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]')
      if (btn) { btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Sending…' }
      errorMsg.classList.add('hidden')

      try {
        const res = await fetch(`https://formspree.io/f/${FORM_ID}`, {
          method: 'POST',
          body: new FormData(form),
          headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },
        })
        if (res.ok) {
          form.classList.add('hidden')
          successMsg.classList.remove('hidden')
          setTimeout(() => { window.location.href = DOWNLOAD_URL }, 1200)
        } else {
          throw new Error()
        }
      } catch {
        if (btn) { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = 'Download the Report →' }
        errorMsg.classList.remove('hidden')
      }
    })
  }
</script>
